Package: boxd-server
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: boxd maintainers <gsalucci@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: podman (>= 5.0), openssh-server, rsync, git, uidmap, catatonit, procps, systemd, socat
Recommends: btrfs-progs, microsandbox-bin, passt
Suggests: zram-tools
Homepage: https://github.com/gsalucci/boxd
Description: build boxes for agents: the build host
 boxd gives coding agents their own build boxes on hardware you own. This
 package is the build host: boxd-pod (the forced command of the build sshd
 that makes and runs one rootless podman container or microsandbox virtual
 machine per agent worktree), boxd-reset, boxd-keepawake, boxctl, boxd-setup,
 the systemd units boxd.service and boxd-sshd.service, and the toolbox image
 sources.
 .
 Installing it changes nothing on the machine. Run boxd-setup as root next: it
 makes the build account, its work area and its ssh key (packaging-debian).
